.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NQP11OPEN 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqp11open ,
.Nm nqp11close ,
.Nm nqp11why ,
.Nm nqp11toks ,
.Nm nqp11login ,
.Nm nqp11keys ,
.Nm nqp11pub ,
.Nm nqp11sign ,
.Nm nqp11dec ,
.Nm nqp11gen ,
.Nm nqp11seal
.Nd keys on a PKCS #11 token
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11open "const char *module" "nqp11 **p"
.Ft void
.Fn nqp11close "nqp11 *p"
.Ft unsigned long
.Fn nqp11why "const nqp11 *p"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11toks "nqp11 *p" "nqp11t *t" "size_t cap" "size_t *n"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11login "nqp11 *p" "unsigned long slot" "const char *pin" "size_t pinlen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11keys "nqp11 *p" "nqp11k *k" "size_t cap" "size_t *n"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11pub "nqp11 *p" "const nqp11k *k" "uint8_t *pk" "size_t cap" "size_t *pklen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11sign "nqp11 *p" "const nqp11k *k" "const uint8_t *msg" "size_t n" "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen" "uint8_t *sig" "size_t cap" "size_t *siglen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11dec "nqp11 *p" "const nqp11k *k" "const uint8_t *ct" "size_t ctlen" "uint8_t *ss" "size_t sslen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11gen "nqp11 *p" "int kem" "int alg" "const char *label" "nqp11k *k"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11seal "nqp11 *p" "const nqp11k *k" "const char *dir" "int fmt" "const char *meta" "const nqcin *in" "size_t nin"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions sign and decapsulate with private keys that stay on a
token: a smart card, a hardware security module, or a software token.
.Pp
HQC keys cannot be made on a token: PKCS #11 3.2 defines no HQC key
type.
.Pp
.Fn nqp11open
loads the PKCS #11 module at the path
.Fa module
and starts it.
The path must have a folder in it; a bare name, which the system
would search for, is refused.
.Fn nqp11close
ends the session, if one is open, and unloads the module.
.Pp
.Fn nqp11toks
lists the tokens present, each an
.Vt nqp11t :
its slot, label, maker, model, serial number, and whether its keys
need the PIN.
.Fn nqp11login
opens a session with the token in
.Fa slot
and, when
.Fa pin
is not
.Dv NULL ,
logs the user in.
A handle has one session.
.Pp
.Fn nqp11keys
lists the private keys noqtis can use, each an
.Vt nqp11k :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef struct {
  int kem;           /* 1: alg is a nqkalg; 0: a nqsalg */
  int alg;
  unsigned long h;   /* the object, in this session */
  char label[65];
  uint8_t id[32];
  size_t idlen;
} nqp11k;
.Ed
.Pp
.Fn nqp11pub
gives the public key of one, in the form
.Xr nqvrfy 3
and
.Xr nqenc 3
take.
.Pp
.Fn nqp11sign
signs
.Fa msg
with a signature key (ML-DSA, SLH-DSA or Ed25519) and the context
.Fa ctx :
the signature is what
.Xr nqsign 3
makes, and
.Xr nqvrfy 3
checks it.
.Fn nqp11dec
decapsulates an ML-KEM ciphertext as
.Xr nqdec 3
does; the module must be of PKCS #11 version 3.2.
.Fn nqp11gen
makes a key pair on the token under
.Fa label ,
the private key marked never to leave it.
.Pp
The mechanisms are those of PKCS #11 version 3.2:
.Dv CKM_ML_DSA
and
.Dv CKM_SLH_DSA
(pure signing; a context goes in a
.Vt CK_SIGN_ADDITIONAL_CONTEXT
with
.Dv CKH_HEDGE_PREFERRED ,
so the token hedges when it can),
.Dv CKM_EDDSA
(Ed25519 with no parameter, Ed25519ctx of RFC 8032 with a
.Vt CK_EDDSA_PARAMS
when there is a context),
.Dv CKM_ML_KEM
for decapsulation, and the matching key-pair generation mechanisms.
A context is at most 255 bytes.
.Fn nqp11gen
marks the private key
.Dv CKA_TOKEN ,
.Dv CKA_PRIVATE
and
.Dv CKA_SENSITIVE
true and
.Dv CKA_EXTRACTABLE
false, and keeps the public key on the token too, both under
.Fa label
and one random
.Dv CKA_ID .
A key pair the token made but then does not describe as the
algorithm asked is destroyed before
.Fn nqp11gen
returns
.Er NQEIO .
.Pp
.Fn nqp11seal
seals the folder
.Fa dir
as
.Xr nqseal 3
does
.Pq Fa fmt No 1
or as
.Fn nqseal2
does
.Pq Fa fmt No 2 , with Fa in No and Fa nin No as there ; for format 1 they are Dv NULL No and 0 ,
with the signature key
.Fa k
of the token.
noqtis never reads the secret key (the token signs); a key made by
.Fn nqp11gen
is marked sensitive and not extractable, and for a key made otherwise
that depends on how it was made.
The manifest is signed on the token with
.Fn nqp11sign ,
the public key written to the seal is the one
.Fn nqp11pub
gives, and the signature is checked under it before anything is
written.
.Fa meta
is the JSON object of the caller's metadata, or
.Dv NULL .
.Pp
A handle is for one thread at a time.
.Pp
In symbols, for
.Fn nqp11seal ,
so that a token seal is the same object as one of
.Xr nqseal 3 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pk  = the public key of the token's key (nqp11pub)
man = the manifest (format 1) or its head (format 2), as nqseal(3)
C_SignInit(session, {CKM_ML_DSA or CKM_SLH_DSA,
           CK_SIGN_ADDITIONAL_CONTEXT{hedge 0, "noqtis-capsule-1"}}, key)
sig = C_Sign(session, man)
written only if Verify(pk, man, sig, "noqtis-capsule-1") holds
.Ed
.Pp
The hedge value 0 asks for a hedged signature when the token can make
one.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK
on success.
.Dv NQEIO
when the module cannot be loaded or the token refuses;
.Fn nqp11why
then gives the module's own return value, a CKR number of the standard.
.Dv NQEDEC
for a library that is not a PKCS #11 module;
.Dv NQEVRFY
for a wrong or locked PIN;
.Dv NQENOSUP
when the token has not the mechanism, for an algorithm PKCS #11 has no
key type for, and on systems that load no shared libraries;
.Dv NQESTATE
before
.Fn nqp11login
or for a second one;
.Dv NQEBUF
with the count or the size needed in
.Fa *n ,
.Fa *pklen
or
.Fa *siglen ;
.Dv NQEARG
for a bad argument and a key of the wrong kind
(for
.Fn nqp11seal ,
a KEM key or a
.Fa fmt
other than 1 and 2).
.Fn nqp11seal
gives also the returns of
.Xr nqseal 3 ,
and
.Dv NQENOSUP
for an Ed25519 key, which alone never seals.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-token 1 ,
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqdec 3 ,
.Xr nqseal 3 ,
.Xr nqsign 3
.Sh STANDARDS
OASIS PKCS #11 Specification Version 3.2.
